title: a1.1 Mindful Walk
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Three scenarios, one per walk. Jan and Elena on the garden loop: a lost thread found again (DS-01). Jan on the phone with Anne: a repeated story, a bench, "Come and get me" (DS-02). Elena alone: "Is Thomas coming today?" (DS-03).

= Design Scenario - Pension day [DS-01] =

//Reimagines PS-01. Realized by UC01. Technology: Pepper at the door (TECH-01), pocket guides (TECH-02), beacons (TECH-03), local server and exchange (TECH-04, TECH-05), walker model (TECH-06).//

Two o'clock. In her room, Elena's guide asks: "A walk with Jan today, or not today?" "With Jan." "May I mention the post office counter to him?" "Yes." At the garden door, Pepper asks Jan alone: "Elena would like a walk with you. Join her, or not today?" "Go on then." "May I mention your post round to Elena?" "Everyone knows that." The map lists nothing off-limits between them; Elena's diagnosis is off-limits with everyone.

Myra clips on both guides and goes back to the ward. Pepper shows two photos: "Jan, this is Elena. Elena, this is Jan." On the path the guides are silent. At the bench: "You both worked for the post, in the same town." Elena: "I had the counter!" She talks about pension day and the queue out of the door, then stops mid-sentence. The guide waits. Jan looks at the pond. After eight seconds, to both: "Elena was telling you about pension day." "The queue! All the way to the bakery." She goes on.

Later Elena says: "My head's no good any more." Jan: "Mine neither. Still got legs, though." They laugh; the guide says nothing. Talking, Jan catches the rollator on the kerb. "Bench on your left." They sit. At twenty-five minutes: "Time to head in. The door is past the roses."

At the door Pepper says: "Welcome back. Pension day, and a queue to the bakery." The record: pair walk, 27 minutes, one stumble, nobody called. Nothing about the conversation.

= Design Scenario - Anne on the line [DS-02] =

//Reimagines PS-02. Realized by UC02. Technology: pocket guide with phone (TECH-02), local server (TECH-04), walker model (TECH-06).//

Anne calls at the agreed time. Jan agreed to walk during calls, and to hints for Anne. The guide: "Anne's calling. Answer?" Jan presses the big button. "It's Anne."

Jan walks the loop and tells the story of the dog that bit the postman. Ten minutes later it starts again. Only Anne hears the guide, a short whisper on the line: "Told before. The roses are out." Anne laughs at the ending, then asks: "Are the roses out yet?" "Red ones, by the bench."

At fifteen minutes Jan has slowed. The guide, to Jan: "Bench on your left. Sit and talk?" Jan sits. "Come and get me, Anne." Anne answers the feeling: "You miss home. I miss you too. I'm coming on Sunday." The guide stays silent.

They say goodbye at twenty minutes. The record: phone walk, 20 minutes, nobody called. Anne calls again that week.

= Design Scenario - Is Thomas coming? [DS-03] =

//Reimagines PS-03. Realized by UC03. Technology: pocket guide (TECH-02), beacons (TECH-03), local server and map (TECH-04, TECH-05), walker model (TECH-06).//

Elena walks the loop alone. She agreed with the coordinator that the guide may talk with her on walks alone. At the door it asked: "May I talk about your garden today?" "Yes."

At the pond: "Ducks on the water." Elena: "Thomas always brought bread for them. Is Thomas coming today?" The map lists Thomas's death as sensitive for Elena: trusted person Myra, approach agreed with her son. The guide: "That's one for Myra. Shall I ask her to come?" "Yes."

Myra's phone: //Elena - asks for Thomas - pond bench.// Myra comes, sits down and answers as agreed with the family: truthfully, gently, and she stays. Elena cries, then talks about Thomas's bicycle. The guide is silent until Myra leaves, then: "The ducks are still there."

The guide does not raise Thomas again. The record: walk alone, 24 minutes, sensitive question, Myra called.

